{"id": "EUVD-2026-82179", "enisaUuid": "1a60fff8-0efa-38e4-8a66-8d59e89dd0dd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nOPP: Fix cleanup ordering\n\nCommit 173e02d67494 (\"OPP: Initialize scope-based pointers inline\")\nadded initialization for all pointers. In some cases, the ordering was\nchanged so that *opp_table was initialized after *opp. This also changes\nthe order of the registered cleanup functions.\n\nWhen the cleanup happens, this can cause use-after-free errors when the\nlast reference is released and the release function _opp_kref_release\ntries to access the already freed opp->opp_table.\n\nInitialize *opp_table before *opp again to fix this and ensure the\ncorrect cleanup order.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:10:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:05:05", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f0c4b7ca24d2e2618a70826881d69b237e36bcc0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ce46fede7792cedd247e34b48bc8a02eb90c7848"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93069", "GHSA-x3pg-c8fj-93pv"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "19095ed8-b038-377f-bb21-2cacad4a7efa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "22fb1143-2f5c-352f-9f60-2108c74a367e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "48513b3b-d817-38a7-bc23-5af2c40b1acf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "173e02d674946ff3ef8da7f44a9d5b820b9af21c <f0c4b7ca24d2e2618a70826881d69b237e36bcc0"}, {"id": "56e738c8-f62d-3dc7-9dda-1688d2d830b2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "b04e9e93-135e-33a8-831d-db7341526c65", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.19"}, {"id": "e7730858-af72-3578-aa36-5b48af42cca9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "173e02d674946ff3ef8da7f44a9d5b820b9af21c <ce46fede7792cedd247e34b48bc8a02eb90c7848"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "528c8b75-645a-3026-87f3-a4cfa812d44f", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}